WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome back to
"Late Night."

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.637
We're here with Jason and Dave.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:08.708
So, gentlemen,
you both have teenagers,

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.077
and I feel like you do
the kind of films

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.213
and the kind of television shows
that teenagers would love,

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.716
but I have often heard from
my friends that, sometimes,

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.685
kids can't separate
the fact that

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.788
it's their parents in shows,
and they don't love them much.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:24.223
Do your kids like
the work you're doing?

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:26.659
-My son could care less.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:32.966
I have not gotten any cool
points for being in movies.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.767
He's more interested
in kind of YouTubers.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.001
He's kind of into that thing.

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:38.805
You know, he's into rappers,
you know, ballers.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.239
He's impressed by that.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.508
Me, not so much, but it's
always kind of been that way.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.377
He grew up with me, you know,
in wrestling.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.512
He was that little baby with me
in the wrestling ring

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.914
and he just kind of
grew up with it,

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.449
and, like, I'm just his dad.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.717
I think, more than anything,
he just wishes I was home more.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:55.321
But, you know, as far as career
goes, no, he's not impressed.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.891
-What about you, Jason?
-My kids love it.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:03.796
And they're on set
with me everywhere.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.999
I mean, you know,
they're friends with everyone.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.934
They love --
It's always Uncle Drax.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:12.638
They love, you know, Affleck
and Gal and, I mean, Ezra.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.407
So, I mean,
they kind of grew up on it.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.343
And thank God,
the first big movie

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.278
that they ever went to
was "Dune."

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:21.481
And it was really
heart-wrenching

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.649
sitting next to my children,

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.016
'cause it was pretty heavy.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:27.954
But they're both like, "This is
my favorite movie, Papa."

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:31.423
So I'm -- It was really special
to take them to that,

00:01:31.423 --> 00:01:35.027
so I'm excited for the world
to see it and --

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.596
But, yeah, I'm still in
the good books, man.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:40.099
-Alright, I'm glad to hear it.
This was very impressive.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:42.101
I guess this was you, Dave.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.704
You basically just -- I think
a lot of people would say

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.006
it's hard to get a
project started in Hollywood.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:50.843
You basically tweeted that
the two of you should do

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:53.613
a "Lethal Weapon"-style movie,

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.316
and it's basically -- everybody
just jumped right on board.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.919
-Yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.354
You know, it's a
new one for me, as well,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.755
and I just kind of put it
out there,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.856
'cause, you know, sometimes,

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.391
I kind of gauge interest
on Twitter.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.826
If you throw
something out there,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.695
people automatically respond
like they're super-hot for it.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.198
'Cause I thought
the idea was great.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.967
And, you know,
I thought it was --

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.002
It really --
You know, Jay is so funny, man.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.805
He's got such a charisma
and such an energy.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.473
but I feel like it hasn't been

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:24.376
on full display
on films or television.

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:25.811
Then I thought about that,
'cause, you know,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.880
we had talked about doing
another project together.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.515
And I thought,
"Man, it would be great

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.317
if the world could see that
side of Jay, man,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:34.153
'cause that side is just --
I mean, it's amazing."

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.189
But I always think
they focus on --

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:39.158
You know, Jay's got such a
great dramatic actor,

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.093
I think that really gets
focused on,

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.929
and they lose sight of,
you know, how funny he is

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:45.264
and how charismatic he is.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.432
And I think it's -- You know,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.833
it's something that
I wanted to be a part of.

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.702
So, anyway, that's how
the idea started with me,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.371
and then I
started thinking about

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.272
the Riggs-and-Murtaugh
relationship,

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:55.007
and I thought
it's perfect for us,

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.909
because he -- I hit him up
and I said,

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.510
"Man, you can be
sexy and charming,

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.046
and I'll just be
old and grouchy.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.681
It's just --
Like, it's perfect."

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.884
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.418
-I will say,
you know, obviously,

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:08.787
we were introduced to you,
a lot of us, Jason,

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:09.822
on "Game of Thrones."

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.157
And you were very serious.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.424
And there was
a photo recently from

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:15.194
David Benioff's birthday
with you and your co-star,

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.664
Emilia Clark, and I think this
is the side of you

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:20.466
that Dave was talking about,
the more fun,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.735
the lighthearted side that we
didn't get to see in

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:26.005
"Game of Thrones."

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.041
-There he is. That's me, Seth.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.544
My favorite show on Earth was
"Saturday Night Live."

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.279
I was raised sitting
next to that TV

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.114
and watching
"Saturday Night Live," yeah.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.749
-The World's about
to see it, man.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:41.921
-Now, I have to ask -- Dave,
obviously, we can see, today --

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.590
We actually have someone who
dresses like you on the show

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.725
named Mike Scollins.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.261
He's a writer.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.963
He has far less impressive arms,

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:54.500
but he is looking to get
his first tattoo.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.637
Dave, what was your first
tattoo, and did you regret it?

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.805
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.408
Yeah, it was -- So,
my first tattoo, you know,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.610
I was -- It was
when I was really young,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.778
and I didn't
want anybody to see it

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.179
and I especially didn't want
my dad to see it.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.747
I didn't want to get into
trouble for getting a tattoo.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:09.882
I was pretty young.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.650
And, so, yeah, it was on my ass.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.052
I got my tattoo on my ass,
and it was just --

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.353
It was really bad.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:18.057
It was just cheesy, and I got it
from this old redneck

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.492
in Arlington, Virginia.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.926
And I told him
where I wanted it,

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:23.495
and he, like, shaved my butt.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:25.431
And then he's, like,
sitting in a rolling chair

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.266
and he rolls up to my face
and he goes,

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.168
"Man, are you sure
you want this on your ass?"

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.637
And I was like --
And I said, "Yeah."

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.005
So he put it there.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:36.108
And like a week or two after
that, I just regretted it.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:37.910
And I lived with it for years.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.779
And I got, you know, ragged
on so much throughout wrestling.

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:43.249
Being in the shower one time was
like, "What's that on your ass?"

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.083
And I was like -- So I finally
got it covered up,

00:04:45.083 --> 00:04:46.719
I think, around 2007.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.654
I just got it covered up
with a --

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.256
-What the hell was it?

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:53.259
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.828
Remember, I was very young.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.463
And this was also the '80s.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:01.434
But it was this,
like, cement-looking heart,

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.469
and around it, it said,
"Heart of stone."

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.705
And when I saw it, I was like,
"Man, that's tough."

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:08.374
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.477
-Heart of stone, man.
I love it.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.946
-I'm still living it down, man.
-Yeah.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:17.617
Also, I was alive in the '80s,
and that wasn't okay then.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:20.853
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.589
"It was the '80s, man."

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.758
-Help me out here, man.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.793
Don't leave me hanging
all by myself here.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.261
Support me on this.

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:31.964
-Hey, I want to thank you both
for being here.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.534
Jason, I want to thank you

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:37.736
for being the one who asked Dave
what the tattoo was.

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:41.240
And thank you so much for making
the time for us today.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.508
It was great
talking to you both.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.976
-Yeah, man. Thank you.
It was a pleasure.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.111
-Be well.

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.079
-The Season 2 finale --
-Momoa!

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:49.449
-The Season 2 finale of "See"

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.084
premieres on Apple TV+
October 15th.

